.TH "PKGEXEC_LINUX_BACKEND" "3" "" "libpkgexec\-linux" "Version 0.6.2"
.SH NAME
pkgexec_linux_backend \- Linux host\-supervisor execution contract
.SH SYNOPSIS
\f[B]#include <libpkgexec\-linux/backend.h>\f[R]
.SH DESCRIPTION
\f[B]host_supervisor_backend::make()\f[R] accepts exact \f[B]interpreter_binding\f[R] values.
The ordinary \f[B]execute()\f[R] overload admits only disabled cancellation.
The controlled overload additionally requires the exact request\-bound \f[B]cancellation_token\f[R].
.PP
The child enters a private session and process group before the final program start gate.
A seccomp filter prevents descendants from changing session, process\-group, namespace, or mount state.
The parent drains requested streams, classifies termination, terminates remaining group members, and reports \f[B]cleanup_verified\f[R] only after the group disappears.
.PP
Cancellation observed before release of the start gate prevents execution.
After start, the backend sends \f[B]SIGTERM\f[R] through pidfds, waits the sealed grace period, and escalates to \f[B]SIGKILL\f[R].
The leader remains unreaped while descendant cleanup is verified.
No ambient signal handler or numeric\-PID cancellation fallback is used.
.PP
This backend creates no alternate filesystem or network view.
It may realize exact address\-space, file\-size, and open\-files limits before the final start gate and seals them against later mutation.
See \f[B]pkgexec_linux_limits\f[R](3) for the limit contract and \f[B]pkgexec_linux_isolated\f[R](3) for private mount\-view execution.
.SH SEE ALSO
